# Context Orchestration Engine - environment template
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Copy this file to '.env' in this directory:   cp .env.example .env
# 2. Uncomment and fill in only the workers you want to run live.
# 3. NEVER commit your real '.env' file or any real key to Git.
#
# Nothing here is needed for the offline mock run: with any worker's key
# missing, `coe run` uses the deterministic mock gateway. Pass --real to force
# live calls.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Worker credentials ------------------------------------------------------
# Each worker in workers.json names the variable it reads via "api_key_env".
# Several workers may share one key: point them at the same variable.
# Left commented on purpose: any non-empty value, even a placeholder, counts
# as a key and turns off the automatic mock fallback.
# WORKER_1_API_KEY=your_worker_1_api_key_here
# WORKER_2_API_KEY=your_worker_2_api_key_here
# WORKER_3_API_KEY=your_worker_3_api_key_here
# WORKER_4_API_KEY=your_worker_4_api_key_here
# WORKER_5_API_KEY=your_worker_5_api_key_here

# --- Gateway -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Live calls go through the built-in standard-library HTTP gateway
# (OpenAI-compatible /chat/completions). To use LiteLLM instead, run
# `pip install litellm` and set:
# COE_GATEWAY=litellm
